Everything under `docs/` — including the wire protocol specification in
`docs/protocol/`, the design and testing documents at the top of this
directory, and the planning material under `docs/superpowers/` — is
licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
(CC BY 4.0).

You are free to:

  - Share — copy and redistribute the material in any medium or format
  - Adapt — remix, transform, and build upon the material

for any purpose, even commercially, as long as you give appropriate credit,
provide a link to the license, and indicate if changes were made.

This single license statement covers the whole directory (there is
deliberately no separate, narrower `docs/protocol/LICENSE` — one statement
avoids the two ever drifting apart). It applies with equal force to the
protocol specification: a specification exists to be implemented by third
parties, so CC BY 4.0 is used here deliberately, instead of a code license,
so that independent client and server implementations of the Relayium wire
protocol are unambiguously permitted and encouraged, with attribution as
the only condition. The same reasoning does no harm applied to the rest of
`docs/` — design notes, testing procedures, and planning records are
likewise meant to be freely reusable with credit, not walled off.

Full license text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
Human-readable summary: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

This license applies only to the documentation in this directory. It does
not apply to the reference implementation of the protocol found in
`server/`, `web/`, and `scripts/` (AGPL-3.0-only) or `apps/` (Apache-2.0),
which are licensed separately — see the root `LICENSE` file for the full
breakdown.
